-- Q4593: Analytical Procedures [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #1, #3
UPDATE questions SET
  choices = $EXPL$["Comparing financial data across periods to identify patterns or fluctuations","Confirming account balances directly with independent third parties","Inspecting supporting documentation for selected individual transactions","Testing the design effectiveness of the entity''s internal controls"]$EXPL$::jsonb,
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Trend analysis is an analytical procedure under AU-C 520 that involves comparing financial data across multiple periods to identify patterns, trends, or unusual fluctuations. It helps the auditor understand performance trajectory and may reveal unexpected changes warranting investigation.
Wrong (B): Confirming balances with third parties is a confirmation procedure, a distinct audit technique from analytical procedures.
Wrong (C): Inspecting supporting documentation is an inspection procedure used in tests of details, not an analytical procedure.
Wrong (D): Testing design effectiveness evaluates internal controls, which is a separate procedure from performing analytical trend analysis.$EXPL$
